{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealSqueeze","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealSqueeze","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealSqueeze.lean#L67-L130","doc":"**surreal_squeeze**: in any `SurrealField K`, for every strictly\npositive infinitesimal `ε ∈ K` and every strictly positive standard\nreal `δ`, the cost `(ofReal δ)² · ε⁻¹` of a standard-scale deviation\nstrictly exceeds the mass-gap budget `ε³`.\n\nThis is the surreal-coefficient version intended by the paper\n(`lem:surreal-squeeze`).  The proof reduces — via\n`surreal_squeeze_of_pow_lt` — to the size separation\n`ε⁴ < (ofReal δ)²`, which holds because `ε⁴` is infinitesimal\n(closure of infinitesimals under multiplication by finite\nelements, applied iteratively) and `(ofReal δ)²` is a strictly\npositive standard real.\n\nRef: [conway1976] https://doi.org/10.1201/9781439864159\nRef: [gonshor1986] https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511629143 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:surreal-squeeze","label":"lem:surreal-squeeze","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_of_pow_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_of_pow_lt","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealSqueeze.lean#L42-L65","doc":"**surreal_squeeze (provable form)**: with the sharper hypothesis\n`ε^4 < δ^2` (which captures the substantive size separation\nbetween standard δ and infinitesimal ε), the conclusion holds in\nany `LinearOrderedField`. This is the form callers should use;\n`surreal_squeeze` above is the loose-hypothesis version that\nrequires a surreal-completion model. ","signatureChunk":0}]}